From ed9e854dd706383c9dbb7fd2a1ac14800f9b628a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harsha Nanda <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 14:52:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(commands): issue-backend selector wiring + registry
 commandOpts (D20)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

resolveCommandOpts strips the selector tokens (--kernel / --issue-backend)
from issue-command args and resolves the backend via the existing backend
authority (lib/issue-backend.js): CLI flag tokens map to its deps.issueBackend
signal, env/config/default precedence comes from the resolver. For the kernel
backend it assembles the driver + migrated broker (B1/B2). executeCommand now
forwards the resolved opts as the handler's 4th arg (defaults to {} —
backward-compatible with existing 3-arg handlers).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
